 1038 #edb/ref 17592186375342 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100818 #edb/ref 1039 "Evaluating Definite Integrals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100818 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186100610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100818 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "37a7aff6-d1b2-5383-bb26-aa6363594b05" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101029 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186101591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101029 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186101592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101029 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186101593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101029 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186101594 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101029 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186101595 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101029 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101029 #edb/ref 1045 "Integrating Logarithmic Functions Using Substitution" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101029 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186101591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101029 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101029 #edb/ref 1050 1080.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186101029 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "0674df03-7c13-5be8-b206-8215c54adc2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101371 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186296944 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101371 #edb/ref 1069 "q-31329" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101371 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101371 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101371 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bc1950d7-cc9c-5e9a-8f86-5dcc05de2e91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101371 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $u={log}_{2}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {log}_{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\cdot \\frac{{log}_{2}^{2}⁡x}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101535 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186100371 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101535 #edb/ref 1069 "q-73654" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101535 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the value of $\\displaystyle \\int_{2}^{4}\\frac{4}{x\\log_{2} x}dx$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101535 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d5cc7305-f37c-53f7-a090-f87a05c29da3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101536 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101536 #edb/ref 1069 "q-73659" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101536 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101536 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\int \\frac{1}{x{log}_{7}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101536 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "15940cb6-48bb-51bb-99eb-a693e64f76c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101536 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $u={log}_{7}⁡(4x).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}\\,⟹\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡7\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{x{log}_{7}⁡(4x)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{log}_{7}⁡(4x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡7\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡7\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{log}_{7}⁡(4x)|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101591 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101591 #edb/ref 1061 118773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101591 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "859100d6-9232-5a35-9f92-1ff67d69671a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101591 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186102029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101592 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101592 #edb/ref 1061 118774 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101592 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3b90fdb1-78e3-5033-ad6e-5d7b6eda947e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101592 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186100816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101593 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101594 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101593 #edb/ref 1061 118778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101593 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bfc6f2ca-3c8f-5042-8e12-9a9d8d3e183b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101593 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186100817 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101594 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101595 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101594 #edb/ref 1061 118782 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101594 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fbecfd22-fc2c-53b8-959b-315e1af4f8fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101594 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186102030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101595 #edb/ref 1061 118783 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101595 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8be2d12d-5050-599a-aca3-294a974cd35b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101595 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186100818 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102029 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's think about how to calculate an integral like $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac {\\ln x} {x} \\,\\textrm d x.$\n\nNotice that this integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\int \\dfrac {\\ln x} {x} \\,\\textrm d x = \\int \\underbrace{\\ln x}_{u} \\cdot\\overbrace{\\dfrac {1} {x}}^{u'} \\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe've seen integrals like this before, where the integrand consists of a function $u(x)$ multiplied by its derivative $u'(x).$ Such integrals can be solved by substitution.\n\nSo, we let $u = \\ln x,$ which gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= \\dfrac 1 x\\quad   \\Longrightarrow \\quad \\dfrac 1 x \\,\\textrm{d}x={\\textrm{d}u}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we can calculate our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n       \\int \\dfrac{\\ln x}{x}\\, \\textrm{d}x \t&=\\int \\ln x\\cdot \\dfrac {1} {x} \\,\\textrm d x \\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t& = \\int u \\, \\textrm{d} u \\[5pt]\n                                                                &=  \\dfrac{1}{2}u^2  +C \\[5pt]   \n                                                                &= \\dfrac{1}{2}\\ln^2 x +C}\n$$\n\nAfter solving an integral using substitution, we should always double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{ln}^{2}x+C) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({ln}^{2}x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[(\\operatorname{ln}x)^{2}]+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{ln}x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x)+0 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}x}{x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102029 #edb/ref 1065 8918 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102029 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "f20c3f56-ce97-548d-a8e0-c4a604acbc18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102029 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102030 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's evaluate the following definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{\\int_{e}^{e^4} \\dfrac{3}{x \\sqrt{\\ln x}} \\, \\textrm{d}x }\n$$\n\nWe'll use the change of variable method, which comprises three steps:\n\n**Step 1:**  Change the variable.\n\nLet's introduce the new variable $u = \\ln x.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{1}{x}\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\\textrm{d}u = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2:**  Find the new limits of integration.\n\nWe use the table below to change our limits of integration from $x$ to $u{:}$\n\n| $x$ | $e$ | $e^4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n\n**Step 3:** Evaluate the integral in the new variable $u.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{3}{x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}x}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{4}{u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6{u}^{1/2}\\,{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =6(\\sqrt{4}-\\sqrt{1}) \\\\  & =6(2-1) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102030 #edb/ref 1065 8931 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102030 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "2add6e6b-5049-58e9-8095-b87e840d0844" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102030 #edb/ref 1067 "Definite Integrals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266165 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{6}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266165 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266165 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "028b5d24-5343-5712-ab0f-d2940e077210" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266302 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}{ln}^{2}⁡x+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266302 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266302 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1254fcec-98e0-5f67-a76b-6f8a8e44308a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266454 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡|x|+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266454 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266454 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2296eb71-af04-5c41-943c-a5d4e6ebc126" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266471 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{12}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266471 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266471 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "238496c5-76bc-51bf-9369-36c9de851713" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266551 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{